[31m-[m
[31m-This backend includes SRM AP email OTP verification for registration, mobile-number/password login, and forgot-password OTP routes.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 1. Keep secrets in your local `.env`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The ZIP intentionally excludes `.env` and `node_modules`. Keep your own local `.env` and configure the following values:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```env[m
[31m-FOODE_EMAIL=your-sender@gmail.com[m
[31m-FOODE_EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your-16-character-google-app-password[m
[31m-SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com[m
[31m-SMTP_PORT=465[m
[31m-SMTP_SECURE=true[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-`FOODE_EMAIL` must be the same Google account that generated the App Password. Use an App Password, not your regular Gmail password. The email service prefers these `FOODE_*` variables; `SMTP_USER` and `SMTP_PASS` are supported only as a legacy fallback. Do not share `.env` or commit it.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 2. Install dependencies[m
[31m-[m
[31m-From the backend directory:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```powershell[m
[31m-npm install[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
